The '''Edgeville Dungeon''' is a [[dungeons|dungeon]] in [[Edgeville]]. It contains a large variety of [[monster]]s spanning across a wide range of levels, as well as the [[Slayer master]] [[Vannaka]]. It can be accessed by a trapdoor south of the Edgeville bank, or a locked shed (requiring a [[Brass key]] to open) west of the [[Cooks' Guild]].

The southern half of the dungeon is [[free-to-play]], and is a popular location for killing [[Hill Giant]]s on free-to-play worlds. The northern half is [[members]]-only, and is in the [[Wilderness]], so anyone who wishes to explore the deeper parts of this dungeon should watch out for [[Player killing|PK'ers]] and only bring items that they are willing to lose. The Members' area is a popular location for killing [[Chaos druid]]s.

The [[Dwarf multicannon|Dwarf Multicannon]] can be used here.

==Transportation==
There are three entrances to the dungeon:
* One is found in [[Edgeville]], in the ruined house south of the [[bank]]. It is a trapdoor by a coffin marked by a dungeon icon ([[File:Dungeon_map_link_icon.png]]) on the minimap. ({{Map|type=maplink|mtype=pin|3097,3469}})
* The other is found in a locked shed west of the [[Cooks' Guild]] near [[Varrock]] on the east side of the [[River Lum]]. To get in, the player must bring a [[brass key]], which can be found in the dungeon. ({{Map|type=maplink|mtype=pin|3116,3452}})
* An [[Obstacle pipe (Edgeville Dungeon)|obstacle pipe]] Agility shortcut from the [[Varrock Sewers]], near [[Bryophyta]]'s lair. ({{Map|type=maplink|mtype=pin|3153,9905|mapID=12}})
Alternatively, the [[Paddewwa Teleport]] on the [[Ancient Magicks]] spellbook can be used to teleport directly into the dungeon.
[[File:Edgeville Dungeon map.png|right|thumb|An annotated map of the Edgeville dungeon.]]
